          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "OAuth callback state is not bound to the initiating user in calendar integration\n\nThe calendar OAuth callback accepts any request that presents a live `state` value and provider `code`, then binds the resulting calendar connection to the victim institute without verifying that the callback caller is the same authenticated administrator who initiated the flow. This allows cross-session callback completion and unauthorized provider-account binding if an attacker obtains a live `state` value before it is consumed."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 91,
                  "endLine": 98,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "class CalendarOAuthStartView(APIView):\n    permission_classes = (IsCurrentInstituteAdmin,)\n\n    def post(self, request):\n        provider = request.data.get(\"provider\")\n        state = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)\n        CalendarOAuthState.objects.create(\n            state=state,\n            institute=request.institute,\n            user=request.user,"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "State creation records the initiating user"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 106,
                  "endLine": 126,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "class CalendarOAuthCallbackView(APIView):\n    permission_classes = (AllowAny,)\n\n    def get(self, request):\n        state = CalendarOAuthState.objects.filter(\n            state=request.query_params.get(\"state\", \"\"),\n            used_at__isnull=True,\n        ).select_related(\"institute\").first()\n        if not state or state.expires_at < timezone.now() or not request.query_params.get(\"code\"):\n            return redirect(...)\n        tokens = exchange_code(state.provider, request.query_params[\"code\"])\n        connection, _ = CalendarIntegrationConnection.objects.update_or_create(\n            institute=state.institute,\n            provider=state.provider,\n            defaults={...},\n        )\n        sync_connection(connection)\n        state.used_at = timezone.now()\n        state.save(update_fields=(\"used_at\",))"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Callback trusts only opaque state and consumes it non-atomically"
              }
            },
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "services/api/modules/school_calendar/models.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 45,
                  "endLine": 69,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "class CalendarIntegrationConnection(models.Model):\n    ...\n    class Meta:\n        constraints = [\n            models.UniqueConstraint(fields=(\"institute\", \"provider\"), name=\"uniq_calendar_connection_provider\"),\n        ]\n\nclass CalendarOAuthState(models.Model):\n    state = models.CharField(max_length=128, unique=True)\n    institute = models.ForeignKey(\"institutes.Institute\", on_delete=models.CASCADE)\n    user = models.ForeignKey(\"identity.User\", on_delete=models.CASCADE)\n    provider = models.CharField(max_length=24, choices=CalendarIntegrationConnection.Provider.choices)\n    expires_at = models.DateTimeField()\n    used_at = models.DateTimeField(null=True, blank=True)"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Recorded initiator is available and connection scope is institute/provider unique"
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/api/v1/admin/calendar/oauth/callback",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "fixes": [
            {
              "artifactChanges": [
                {
                  "artifactLocation": {
                    "uri": "services/api/modules/school_calendar/api/views.py"
                  },
                  "replacements": [
                    {
                      "deletedRegion": {
                        "startLine": 106,
                        "endLine": 126
                      },
                      "insertedContent": {
                        "text": "class CalendarOAuthCallbackView(APIView):\n    permission_classes = (IsAuthenticated,)\n\n    def get(self, request):\n        state = CalendarOAuthState.objects.select_for_update().filter(\n            state=request.query_params.get(\"state\", \"\"),\n            used_at__isnull=True,\n            user=request.user,\n        ).select_related(\"institute\").first()\n        if not state or state.expires_at < timezone.now() or not request.query_params.get(\"code\"):\n            return redirect(...)\n\n        state.used_at = timezone.now()\n        state.save(update_fields=(\"used_at\",))\n\n        tokens = exchange_code(state.provider, request.query_params[\"code\"])\n        connection, _ = CalendarIntegrationConnection.objects.update_or_create(\n            institute=state.institute,\n            provider=state.provider,\n            defaults={...},\n        )\n        sync_connection(connection)"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "description": {
                "text": "1. Require the callback to complete in the same authenticated application session that initiated the OAuth flow, rather than treating possession of the opaque `state` value as sufficient authorization.\n2. Compare the authenticated callback principal to `CalendarOAuthState.user` before exchanging the provider `code` or updating any institute connection.\n3. Consume the state atomically before token exchange and synchronization so concurrent callbacks cannot reuse the same live state.\n4. Fail closed when the callback is unauthenticated, when the authenticated user does not match the recorded initiator, or when the state has already been consumed.\n5. Consider binding the state to a signed nonce stored in the user's authenticated session in addition to the database row.",
                "markdown": "1. Require the callback to complete in the same authenticated application session that initiated the OAuth flow, rather than treating possession of the opaque `state` value as sufficient authorization.\n2. Compare the authenticated callback principal to `CalendarOAuthState.user` before exchanging the provider `code` or updating any institute connection.\n3. Consume the state atomically before token exchange and synchronization so concurrent callbacks cannot reuse the same live state.\n4. Fail closed when the callback is unauthenticated, when the authenticated user does not match the recorded initiator, or when the state has already been consumed.\n5. Consider binding the state to a signed nonce stored in the user's authenticated session in addition to the database row."
              }
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "95a9cac6be299c97917938ecd7f221f6b2569e37c4274a9d1928c24ec60aef66"
